Z||000001||87GT||06-27-99||04:41 PM|||| I know that fever.  I caught that fever in the spring of 1998.  I went with some friends to the Daytona car show at the speedway.  We stayed at a Holiday Inn where it just so happen there was a Fiero club meet.  I saw so many of little things that my head began to spin.  I had always known of the Fiero but didnt pay much attention to them.  While at the Holiday Inn, I began looking at these cars.  The morning after, they all were headed to the speedway and I was just amazed at the unique beauty of these cars.  I had to have one after that.  I sold my 94 Grand Prix and bought my first fiero which of course, is a 87GT with 86,000 miles on it.  I love it to death and just got done washing it just a few minutes ago. LOL!  Well, that is the story of me catching the fever.  It's very contagious!
Z||000002||yellowFormula||06-27-99||07:17 PM||||That's a great story 87GT, I think we can all relate to the fiero 'fever'.  I got it during the winter of 97 when my sisters boyfriend at the time bought a 84 coupe in perfect condition (even had original floormats!) That was it for me , I was hooked.  Before then I had never even heard of Fiero's (I'm young, give me a break). I then began searching the internet for more info. After I discovered all the info I could get from the internet I decided I wanted a 88 Formula.  For some reason the 86-88 GT body style just isn't as appealing to me as the notchback, and the best stock notchback is the Formula as we all know.  So then my search began, and I didn't find a Formula that matched my search criteria until about 2 and a half months ago (good things come to those who wait).  Since then I found another formula for dirt cheap. So thats my Fiero story, if anyone cares. 
