Z||000009||lowCG||07-01-99||06:29 PM||||Sounds to me like the last four(4) posts have S.S.S.(Stock Suspension Syndrome).<br>I too was once a sufferer,then,realizing that the only person to help me was indeed myself,I set out on a mission to achieve superior handling to satisfy my discriminating tastes,and to "one up" my friends who(probably laughing at me)drive TurboPorsches,Ferraris,and who road race motorcycles.<br>I have the recipe for those interested;don't claim to have the highest skidpad rating,I don't drive on perfectly smooth skidpads,but for the real world it's hard to beat.Car will generally feel vague going down the raod,but,feed it to a corner,and as you begin to feel the G forces gradually build,you eventually will get a breakaway that is very gradual,controllable,giving plenty of time to respond to the generous feedback,steering with the throttle as well as the wheel.<br>
