Z||000011||lowCG||07-01-99||10:01 PM||||Your springs are just stock,that's all,Pontiac never was a sportscar company.<br>The twitch you feel coming on is uncontrolled movement/inertia, rapidly followed by a too stiff situation,where you then could very quickly begin to slide/rotate.Excessive rear toe-in will make things swing out a little faster too.<br>Herb Adams made some springs that were plain stiff, fun,I suppose if you're on a smooth track with slicks,nerves of steel.One guy I know of cracked his windshield using a set of these!<br>By the way,Will,you have a cool car now!<br>Congradulations.
